Hello, my name is **Pixel (@pixelkat05 on Discord)**, and I am the **Team Leader for the 3D Team**!

Before continuing with this doc, please read the [General Onboarding Document](/guides/onboardings/general-onboarding/).

---

## What We Do

The 3D team is a combo of modders/rippers of Persona games + 3D modellers, & is responsible for creating the 3D assets (environments, character models, etc.) used in the game.

### [p3d-amicitia](https://github.com/p3d-project/p3d-amicitia)

P3D Amicitia (a fork of [Amicitia](https://github.com/tge-was-taken/Amicitia)) is an editor for file formats used in Atlus' Persona games, modified by member(s) of the P3D team in hopes of an easier workflow

---

## Contributions

The process of assigning tasks is self-directed. You'll need to select a task from the [GitHub Project Board](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22) under **“Ready”** & assign yourself & assign yourself. Sometimes, team leads will ask you to do some issues as well.

Once you have finished, please share photos/videos of the completed asset to the #3d-lounge for feedback. Once we've given the OK, you can upload the files to the 3D team’s folder in [Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1FAb7dC2GPEaNTfF5tSxioYkLp6wkU7tT?usp=drive_link), where the Game Dev team can place them into the game files.

Make sure that you strictly follow the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing). If you want to work on an issue that isn’t on the roadmap, make sure you get approval from the team lead (pixelkat05) or the project lead (thebosst). If you want to work on an issue that IS on the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing), find the associated GitHub issue! If you can’t find it, feel free to make a new issue under the “New” tab.

All new 3D team members must also read [3D Team Reference](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hmnpGXq6uIHmftyvrVKXXZp6ufZb6BM4zbltL7y3FNQ/edit?usp=sharing) & [Art Standards](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hFSdY6zVBxsenvYRairC2hBy67O43v8J6SDU-CjzxdM/edit?usp=sharing).

---

### Limitations

- We need to make our own 3D models (cannot use ripped 3D models)
- Models need to fit within the vertex count (6,144 vertices) for the DS
- Right now, roughly ~1k vertices are taken up by the current (bad) character model.
- We can have more vertices in an environment, it's just that the DS can only render 6,144 vertices at one time
- We want to get the vertex count down as much as possible, while still making the environment/models itself look decent

---

## AI Usage Policy

- There will be **NO** usage of Generative AI within the 3D Team. Anyone found to be using it to produce assets for the project will be kicked from the team, and have their contributions removed.

---

## Tools & Setup

The team uses [Blender](https://www.blender.org/) for modelling, & other various tools for ripping assets from games.

